  "diagnostic_correction": "The new all-pairs cost-radius test initially exposed an unclamped unreachable component when reverse BFS exhausted before its horizon. The final implementation initializes the clamp to C+1 and passes all source/sink/radius consistency checks before v4 native runs.",
  "conclusions": [
    "All tested corridor modes are electrically legal in the qualified native graph and repeat deterministically; none uses the flat fallback on this cohort.",
    "All corridor final trees have 2745 PIPs versus direct baseline 2528 (+8.58%); selected SLL count stays 36. These counts do not establish physical wirelength or timing QoR.",
    "Unbounded new-entry comparison finds zero better candidates and expands 79429148 nodes per repeat. Cost bounds reduce this to 8358857, but preparing uncapped quotient potentials is expensive.",
    "Quotient cost-radius truncation reduces that preparation from 1042931121 to 174492512 expanded groups (83.27%) with complete candidate/shadow journals unchanged. Even the final mode does not establish a speedup over the direct baseline.",
    "Current reservations are serial candidate-local records with negotiated overuse, not strict concurrent hardware grants."
  ],
